        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "For a paragraph more than five or six sentences long, underline the sentence that you think best introduces or frames the rest of the paragraph. If you can't do that quickly, the paragraph probably has a problem. If you can, circle the important words in the sentence. Those words should sound like a title for the paragraph. If they do not, your paragraph may confuse your readers. We will return to this matter in Lesson 7.",
            "block_bbox": [
                115,
                506,
                771,
                625
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
