        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Read a page of your own writing aloud, raising your voice and tapping your fingers at the ends of your sentences (as suggested in the Quick Tip on page 77). What do you notice? How often do you seem to be stressing the wrong words and how often the right ones? Can you detect any patterns? How does your meaning change when you inadvertently stress the wrong words?",
            "block_bbox": [
                115,
                790,
                771,
                909
